      "body": "**Actionable comments posted: 15**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>src/components/CardForm.tsx (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`52-55`: _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**CVC `onChange`도 도메인 값 중심 인터페이스로 맞추는 것이 좋습니다.**\n\n현재 CVC만 DOM 이벤트를 부모로 노출하고 있어( Line 54 ) 카드번호/유효기간과 API 형태가 다릅니다. 상위 폼이 이벤트 구조에 결합되지 않도록 `string` 값을 직접 전달하는 형태로 맞춰보세요.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardForm.tsx` around lines 52 - 55, CardCVCInput의 onChange가 현재\nDOM 이벤트(e) 를 부모에 전달하는데 카드번호/만료일 처리와 API가 다른 형태로 결합됩니다; 변경할 때는 부모에 문자열 값만 전달하도록\nCardCVCInput 사용 지점을 수정하여 onChange={(value: string) => props.setFormState({\n...props.formState, cvc: value })} 형태로 바꾸고, 참조되는 심볼은 CardCVCInput,\nprops.formState.cvc, props.setFormState이며 부모 컴포넌트가 이벤트 객체 대신 순수 string 값을 받도록\n조정하세요.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>package.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-13`: **`gh-pages`를 `devDependencies`에 추가하여 배포 스크립트의 재현성을 개선하세요.**\n\nLine 13의 `npx gh-pages -d dist`는 선언된 의존성 없이 외부에서 직접 해석되므로 환경에 따라 버전 불일치가 발생할 수 있습니다. `package.json`의 `devDependencies`에 `gh-pages`를 추가하고 스크립트에서 직접 실행하도록 정리하면 팀 전체와 CI에서 일관된 배포가 가능합니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@package.json` at line 13, 현재 package.json의 \"deploy\" script uses npx gh-pages\nwhich can lead to version drift; add \"gh-pages\" to package.json devDependencies\nand update the script to call the local binary (e.g., change \"deploy\" to run\ngh-pages -d dist after build). Concretely: add \"gh-pages\" to devDependencies\n(install with npm/yarn as a dev dependency) and modify the \"deploy\" script value\n(the \"deploy\" key in package.json) to use the installed gh-pages binary instead\nof npx so CI and teammates use the pinned version.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for all review comments with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nInline comments:\nIn `@README.md`:\n- Around line 7-28: The README checklist currently shows every item as unchecked\nwhich misrepresents implementation status; update the checklist under the \"카드 번호\n입력\", \"카드 유효기간 입력\", \"CVC\", \"실시간 프리뷰 업데이트\" and \"프로그래밍 요구 사항\" sections to reflect\nactual implementation by toggling individual checkboxes to [x] for completed\nitems and leaving [ ] for pending ones (e.g., mark completed features such as\n4-input card number handling, numeric-only validation, storybook setup, or\nerror-handling refactors accordingly), and optionally add a short status note or\nversion/date line near the checklist to indicate when it was last updated so\nreaders can tell which items are implemented vs outstanding.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardExpiryDateInput.tsx`:\n- Line 97: Fix the typo in the validation error message inside\nCardExpiryDateInput (the message string currently reading '유효한 년도을 입력해주세요. (00 ~\n99)'); change it to '유효한 년도를 입력해주세요. (00 ~ 99)' so the grammar is correct.\nLocate the message property in the validation logic within\nCardExpiryDateInput.tsx and update that string accordingly.\n- Around line 20-33: CardExpiryDateInput currently initializes local state\n(expiryMonth, expiryYear) from props.value and syncs via useEffect, causing\ndesync when parent updates; remove the local useState/useEffect and make the\ncomponent fully controlled by props.value: delete expiryMonth/expiryYear state\nand the useEffect, and update handleChangeMonth and handleChangeYear to call\nprops.onChange with the new month/year combined with props.value.expiryYear or\nprops.value.expiryMonth respectively (e.g., props.onChange([newMonth,\nprops.value.expiryYear]) and props.onChange([props.value.expiryMonth, newYear]))\nso the inputs read directly from props.value and changes propagate to the\nparent.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardForm.tsx`:\n- Around line 20-23: CardFormProps currently types setFormState as (value:\nCardFormState) => void which can cause lost updates; change its type to\nDispatch<SetStateAction<CardFormState>> and update all state updates in the\nCardForm component (where you spread props.formState at the handlers referenced\naround lines 36, 46, 54) to use the functional update form setFormState(prev =>\n({ ...prev, <changedFields> })) so each handler reads the previous state and\nmerges changes instead of spreading props.formState directly.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardNumberSegmentsInput.tsx`:\n- Around line 14-25: 컴포넌트가 props.value를 초기값으로만 사용해 부모에서 값이 바뀌어도 동기화되지 않으니 완전\n제어형으로 변경하세요: 내부 state인 segments 및 setSegments를 제거하고 컴포넌트는 항상 props.value를 사용하도록\n하며 handleChange에서는 새로운 배열을 생성해 props.onChange(updatedSegments)를 호출하도록 변경(즉\nuseEffect로 부모에만 통지하는 대신 props.value를 단일 출처로 사용). 관련 심볼: segments, setSegments,\nprops.value, useEffect, handleChange, props.onChange.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardPreview.tsx`:\n- Around line 43-44: The CardImage elements currently render without alt text,\nharming screen-reader accessibility; update the CardImage usages in CardPreview\n(the two occurrences rendering `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}chip.svg` and\n`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}${props.cardBrand.toLowerCase()}.svg`) to include\nappropriate alt attributes: for purely decorative chip.svg use alt=\"\" and for\nthe brand image use a descriptive alt like `${props.cardBrand} logo` (or an\nempty string if decorative), ensuring the alt value derives from props.cardBrand\nand is passed as the alt prop to the CardImage component.\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/Flex.tsx`:\n- Around line 17-18: The conditional that outputs flex-grow and flex-shrink uses\nprops.gap, so passing only flexGrow or flexShrink is ignored; in the Flex styled\ncomponent update the two lines that currently check (props) => (props.gap ? ...)\nto instead check the specific props (e.g., (props) => (props.flexGrow != null ?\n`flex-grow: ${props.flexGrow};` : '') and similarly for flexShrink) so each\nstyle is emitted when its own prop is provided (use != null to allow 0 values).\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/InputErrorMessage.tsx`:\n- Around line 6-8: The InputErrorMessage component currently uses a fixed height\n(\"height: 14px\") which causes UI overlap for long error texts; update the\nstyling in InputErrorMessage (the styled/component CSS block that contains\nline-height, height, margin) to replace the fixed height with a min-height\n(e.g., min-height: 14px) and ensure text can wrap (confirm word-wrap/white-space\ndefaults allow wrapping), so the element can grow for longer messages without\noverlapping.\n\nIn `@src/components/Common/ValidationInput.tsx`:\n- Line 25: The ValidationInput component is spreading custom props\n(onChangeError, isShowError) into the DOM via the Input styled component; update\nthe function signature to explicitly destructure onChangeError and isShowError\nfrom the props (e.g., ValidationInput({ validations, onChange, onBlur,\nonChangeError, isShowError, ...props })) and then pass only the remaining\n...props into <Input {...props} /> so non-standard attributes are not forwarded\nto the DOM.\n- Line 47: In handleOnBlur, replace usage of props.value with event.target.value\nso the validation uses the actual input from the blur event (matching\nhandleOnChange's event.target.value); update the validation logic inside the\nhandleOnBlur function to read from event.target.value and ensure any calls that\nrely on the current input (e.g., validation functions or setError/setTouched\ncalls) use that value instead of props.value.\n\nIn `@src/hooks/useCardBrand.ts`:\n- Line 6: The regex in useCardBrand.ts uses the global flag with RegExp.test (if\n(/^(51)|(52)|(53)|(54)|(55)/g.test(CardNumberSegments[0]))), which makes the\nRegExp stateful and can produce incorrect results on repeated calls; remove the\n`g` flag (or create a new RegExp each call without `g`) so the test is\nstateless, e.g., update the check in the function that references\nCardNumberSegments[0] to use /^(51|52|53|54|55)/.test(...) or instantiate a\nfresh RegExp without the `g` flag before calling .test().\n\nIn `@src/stories/CardPreview.stories.tsx`:\n- Around line 23-25: The expiryYear control in CardPreview.stories.tsx is\ndefined as type 'number' but the CardPreview component and all story args expect\na string; change the control for expiryYear from a numeric control to a\nstring/text control (e.g., control: { type: 'text' }) so the story injects a\nstring value that matches the component prop and the description; update the\nexpiryYear control definition in the CardPreview.stories.tsx controls object\n(the expiryYear entry) to use a text/string control.\n\nIn `@src/stories/ValidationInput.stories.tsx`:\n- Line 1: The file uses React.ComponentProps (e.g., React.ComponentProps on line\n23) but never imports the React namespace, causing a TS compile error; fix this\nby adding a top-level React namespace import such as import React from 'react';\n(or import type * as React from 'react' if you prefer type-only import) so that\nReact.ComponentProps resolves correctly—add the import alongside the existing\nimport { useState } from 'react'; and keep other code unchanged.\n\nIn `@src/styles/index.css`:\n- Around line 1-2: CI fails due to Stylelint import-notation rule because the\nstylesheet uses `@import` url(...) syntax; replace those `@import` url(...)\noccurrences with string import notation (e.g., `@import` \"reset.css\"; and `@import`\n\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/...\";) so the imports use plain string literals\ninstead of url(...) to satisfy the import-notation rule.\n\nIn `@src/utils.ts`:\n- Around line 1-3: validateNumberString currently treats whitespace as numeric\nbecause Number(' ') === 0; update the validation to accept only digits 0-9 (and\nreject spaces, signs, decimals) by replacing the per-char Number check with a\ndigit-only test (e.g., use a regex like ^[0-9]+$ or test each char with /\\d/),\nand ensure empty strings are handled according to desired behavior (reject if\nyou want at least one digit).\n\n---\n\nNitpick comments:\nIn `@package.json`:\n- Line 13: 현재 package.json의 \"deploy\" script uses npx gh-pages which can lead to\nversion drift; add \"gh-pages\" to package.json devDependencies and update the\nscript to call the local binary (e.g., change \"deploy\" to run gh-pages -d dist\nafter build). Concretely: add \"gh-pages\" to devDependencies (install with\nnpm/yarn as a dev dependency) and modify the \"deploy\" script value (the \"deploy\"\nkey in package.json) to use the installed gh-pages binary instead of npx so CI\nand teammates use the pinned version.\n\nIn `@src/components/CardForm.tsx`:\n- Around line 52-55: CardCVCInput의 onChange가 현재 DOM 이벤트(e) 를 부모에 전달하는데 카드번호/만료일\n처리와 API가 다른 형태로 결합됩니다; 변경할 때는 부모에 문자열 값만 전달하도록 CardCVCInput 사용 지점을 수정하여\nonChange={(value: string) => props.setFormState({ ...props.formState, cvc: value\n})} 형태로 바꾸고, 참조되는 심볼은 CardCVCInput, props.formState.cvc, props.setFormState이며 부모\n컴포넌트가 이벤트 객체 대신 순수 string 값을 받도록 조정하세요.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪄 Autofix (Beta)</summary>\n\nFix all unresolved CodeRabbit comments on this PR:\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"4b0d0e0a-96d7-4f10-b296-3a18ea78f0b9\"} --> Push a commit to this branch (recommended)\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"ff5b1114-7d8c-49e6-8ac1-43f82af23a33\"} --> Create a new PR with the fixes\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>ℹ️ Review info</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⚙️ Run configuration</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: Organization UI\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n**Run ID**: `8d160c4f-32db-40c5-93ec-c120187fd9c2`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 8d4c2c73f7cce87ffaae55245ae1cfd10228981d and 6197e18805ee